.TH X11-MAGNIFIER 1 "2026-11-19" "x11-magnifier" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
x11-magnifier \- full-screen magnifier for X11
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B x11-magnifier
[\fB\-c\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-m\fR \fIMODS\fR] [\fB\-s\fR \fISTEP\fR] [\fB\-M\fR \fIMAX\fR] [\fB\-e\fR \fIPX\fR] [\fB\-r\fR \fIMS\fR] [\fB\-p\fR] [\fB\-n\fR] [\fB\-i\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs in the background and grabs modifier+scroll on the X root window.
Scrolling up zooms the whole screen in around the pointer; pushing the pointer
against a screen edge pans the view; scrolling down zooms out and, at 1.0x,
removes the magnified view. A mouse click also leaves the zoomed view.
The view live-updates: windows are redirected with the Composite extension and
repainted on XDamage events.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " FILE"
Config file. Default ~/.config/x11-magnifier/config. Flags override it.
.TP
.BI \-m " MODS"
Modifiers joined by +: ctrl, shift, alt, super. Default ctrl+shift.
.TP
.BI \-s " STEP"
Zoom factor per scroll tick. Default 1.08.
.TP
.BI \-M " MAX"
Maximum zoom. Default 12.
.TP
.BI \-e " PX"
Edge-pan margin in pixels. Default 40.
.TP
.BI \-r " MS"
Minimum milliseconds between live refreshes. Default 200.
.TP
.B \-p
Plain static snapshot, no live refresh.
.TP
.B \-n
Nearest-neighbour scaling instead of bilinear.
.TP
.B \-i
Invert scroll direction (natural scrolling).
.SH CONFIGURATION
The config file has one "key = value" per line; # starts a comment. Keys:
modifiers, step, max_zoom, edge_margin, refresh_ms, live, nearest,
invert. An annotated example is installed in /usr/share/doc/x11-magnifier/examples/.
.SH NOTES
The chosen modifier+scroll combination is grabbed system-wide while the
program runs. If another client already holds it, x11-magnifier exits with an error.
